WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.087
There are four Spark terms I want you to recognize.

00:00:05.087 --> 00:00:07.887
A partition is one piece of a larger dataset.

00:00:07.887 --> 00:00:12.862
A task is a unit of work that processes a partition.

00:00:12.862 --> 00:00:19.872
A stage is a group of tasks that can run before Spark needs to reorganize the data.

00:00:19.872 --> 00:00:24.162
A shuffle is the movement of data between workers.

00:00:24.162 --> 00:00:24.777
Here is the key idea.

00:00:24.777 --> 00:00:33.192
Parallel processing is helpful when workers can operate on separate pieces of data.

00:00:33.192 --> 00:00:38.902
It becomes more expensive when the workers must exchange large amounts of data.

00:00:38.902 --> 00:00:43.930
That is why the word shuffle will come up repeatedly in this module.
